      "highlights": "the Chairman & Managing Director and the Deputy Managing Director: Our company was founded on a simple conviction: that Indian farmers and builders deserved machinery built with the same rigour and care as anywhere in the world. FY 2025-26 is proof that this conviction was right, and that it continues to compound. The bygone year witnessed strong momentum across the agricultural machinery sector, supported by favourable rural conditions, continued policy support, and sustained progress in farm mechanisation. At the same time, it reinforced an important reality: growth in the sectors where we operate remains inherently cyclical, shaped by shifts in agriculture, infrastructure creation, policy direction, technology adoption, and evolving customer aspirations. FY 2025–26 was a defining year for Demo Manufacturing. The year was marked by strong operating performance, continued premiumisation, and sharper strategic focus. We strengthened our market position, accelerated export momentum, and took decisive steps to streamline our portfolio. The divestment of the Railway Equipment Division enabled us to unlock value and redirect capital toward core growth areas. We also continued to build on the amalgamation of our two Demo Manufacturing joint ventures into DML, with 'One DML' now firmly embedded as an operating reality and beginning to deliver tangible synergies across operations, products, and processes; Sustainability transcends compliance at Demo Manufacturing; it is embedded in our operational DNA and long-term strategy. We have implemented comprehensive ESG frameworks across water conservation, renewable energy adoption in manufacturing, and circular economy practices for equipment lifecycle management. Our factories now feature solar power integration and upgrading to zeroliquid discharge systems, delivering both environmental stewardship and cost efficiencies. Our community initiatives focus on skill development for rural youth, women empowerment through Agri‑entrepreneurship programmes, and farmer producer organisation support. These efforts create shared value, strengthening rural ecosystems while building brand equity. Our Great Place to Work certification reflects our commitment to employee wellbeing, diversity, and inclusive growth, ensuring we attract and retain top talent for sustained innovation."
