      "highlights": "DML is progressively strengthening its ESG Landscape through a structured and phased approach that aligns sustainability with governance, risk management, and long-term strategy. Building on this foundation, DML has established policies covering key areas such as climate change, human rights and sustainable procurement, which are embedded within its Code of Conduct and Supplier Code of Conduct to guide ethical and responsible business practices. These policies are aligned with global standards (including IFRS S1 & S2, UNGP, and ILO) and aim to embed climate risk management, responsible sourcing, and lowcarbon decision-making into operations. Further, the Company plans to expand its policy framework in coming year addressing emerging priorities such as biodiversity, water management, circular economy, and sustainable agriculture. Alongside these, DML’s existing policies, including Code of Conduct, Risk Management, EHS, CSR, and data protection frameworks, are aligned with the National Guidelines on Responsible Business Conduct (NGRBC), ensuring comprehensive ESG oversight. Overall, this layered and forward-looking policy landscape reflects DML’s commitment to embedding ESG considerations across its value chain and enhancing sustainable value creation."
