      "metrics": [],
      "highlights": "DML has articulated a comprehensive set of planet-focused commitments aimed at driving long-term environmental sustainability and climate resilience. The Company is advancing its climate neutrality agenda by aligning with the Science Based Targets initiative (SBTi) and the 1.5°C pathway, supported by efforts in decarbonisation, energy efficiency, and renewable energy adoption, with a longterm goal of achieving Carbon Neutrality by FY 2049-50. As part of its energy transition strategy, DML is increasing the share of renewable energy, particularly through solar installations and clean energy initiatives. The Company is also working towards becoming water positive by FY 2029-30, focusing on water efficiency, recycling, and stewardship, while aiming to achieve zero waste to landfill by FY 2026-27 through improved waste management practices. In addition, DML is embedding circular economy principles by expanding sustainable and low-carbon product offerings and increasing their contribution to revenue. Further, DML is strengthening its focus on biodiversity and nature-related risks, progressing towards structured assessments and alignment with emerging global frameworks. Overall, these commitments reflect a holistic approach to environmental sustainability, integrating climate action, resource efficiency, and nature stewardship into the Company’s longterm strategy."
