      "highlights": "DML is progressively strengthening its ESG Landscape through a structured and phased approach that aligns sustainability with governance, risk management, and long-term strategy. Building on this foundation, DML has established policies covering key areas such as climate change, human rights and sustainable procurement, which are embedded within its Code of Conduct and Supplier Code of Conduct to guide ethical and responsible business practices. These policies are aligned with global standards (including IFRS S1 & S2, UNGP, and ILO) and aim to embed climate risk management, responsible sourcing, and lowcarbon decision-making into operations; The organisation undertakes scenario analysis across different climate pathways to assess potential financial impacts over the short, medium, and long term, enabling informed risk management and strategic planning."
