      "highlights": "Enterprise Risk Management (ERM) at DML refers to the holistic and continuous process of identifying, assessing, managing, and monitoring risks across the organisation to ensure the achievement of strategic and operational objectives. It is embedded within business decision-making and covers all categories of risks, including strategic, operational, financial, and compliance risks. ERM enables the Company to proactively address uncertainties, improve resilience, and enhance performance by aligning risk-taking with defined risk appetite. Through structured governance involving the Board, Risk Management Committee, Chief Risk Officer, and Risk Owners, ERM ensures accountability, transparency, and integration of risk considerations into everyday operations and long-term planning. The organisation undertakes scenario analysis across different climate pathways to assess potential financial impacts over the short, medium, and long term, enabling informed risk management and strategic planning."
