      "highlights": "Advancing Emission-Compliant Technologies in Engines: DML transitioned from BS IV to BS V emission standards in its construction equipment portfolio, strengthening compliance with evolving environmental regulations. The Company introduced Diesel Particulate Filter (DPF) systems, co-developed with Demo Manufacturing engineers, to reduce emissions and meet regulatory norms. DML also launched CPCB4+ compliant engines for the genset market, transitioning from mechanical to electronic control systems. These advancements enhance emission performance while enabling future integration of smart diagnostics and engine control technologies. DML is advancing hybrid and electric solutions, including diesel-CNG hybrid cranes and electric tractor pilots, with plans to scale adoption over the next 2–5 years in line with market and environmental readiness."
