      "highlights": "DML follows a structured approach to biodiversity and ecosystem conservation, guided by a no-net-loss principle, with a focus on minimising ecological impact and supporting restoration where feasible. These principles are integrated into sustainability decisionmaking and extended across the value chain. This approach is embedded within DML’s broader environmental stewardship, encompassing carbon reduction, clean energy use, water and waste management, and responsible natural resource use, supported by engagement across stakeholders. DML is further strengthening its biodiversity management by aligning with evolving global frameworks and advancing nature-related disclosures. Efforts are underway to establish a biodiversity baseline through structured assessments and group-level alignment with emerging standards. With respect to ecologically sensitive areas, the Company does not have operations in or around such regions. Accordingly, there are no significant direct or indirect impacts on biodiversity requiring specific prevention or remediation measures. On-ground initiatives include tree plantations and urban forestation programmes in partnership with government authorities. In FY 2025–26, projects such as Namo Van led to the plantation of 1,00,000 saplings, supported by ongoing maintenance and monitoring to enhance ecological outcomes."
