      "highlights": "DML embeds circularity into product and material strategies—designing for durability and recyclability, and increasing use of secondary materials where feasible. We are scaling low‑carbon and sustainable product solutions to grow revenue from such offerings; Demo Manufacturing Limited partnered with Green Globecare to recycle waste paper generated across its Faridabad facilities during April 2025-March 2026. This initiative aligns with the Environment (Protection) Act, 1986 and supports the company’s ESG commitments. Key Results: Total Waste Paper Recycled: 11,240 kg; Trees Saved: 191.08; Water Conserved: 78,680 litres; Energy Saved: 44,960 kWh; GHG Emission Reduced: 16,860 kg; Carbon Credit Equivalent: 16.86 metric tons CO2 reduction; The Company plans to expand its policy framework in coming year addressing emerging priorities such as biodiversity, water management, circular economy, and sustainable agriculture."
