      "highlights": "Driving Sustainable Impact: DML’s sustainability approach is anchored around a three-pillar ESG framework comprising Planet, People, and Governance. The framework guides the Company’s approach towards responsible growth, operational resilience, stakeholder value creation, and long-term sustainability integration across business operations and the value chain. Our Three-Pillar Framework: The framework is aligned with the Company’s Strategic Objectives (SO1–SO5) and linked to identified material sustainability topics (M1–M16), enabling focused action across key ESG priorities; DML’s People Commitments focus on building an inclusive, safe, and future-ready workforce while creating meaningful social impact. The Company is advancing its diversity, equity and inclusion (DE&I) to 15% in employee category by FY 2030-31, while strengthening employee well-being, health and safety, capability development and community engagement. Improving gender diversity in operational roles and advancing ESG integration across the value chain remain key priorities. DML maintains a strong commitment to health, safety, and well-being, aiming for zero fatalities while continuously improving occupational safety standards and expanding well-being and mental health initiatives. At the same time, the Company is investing in talent development through structured learning programmes, leadership development initiatives, and global knowledge-sharing platforms to build future-ready capabilities across all levels; Human Capital forms the foundation of our long-term success. At DML, we are committed to strengthening the employee lifecycle through strategic talent acquisition, continuous capability development, and performance-driven practices. By fostering an inclusive, equitable, and supportive workplace, while prioritising employee well-being and future-ready skills, we seek to build a resilient, agile, and high-performing workforce that supports our growth ambitions and creates lasting value."
