      "highlights": "DML maintains structured and accessible grievance redressal mechanisms for employees and workers across categories, supported by dedicated committees and defined processes. These systems enable timely, fair, and transparent resolution of concerns while upholding confidentiality and non-retaliation. An Ethics Committee and formal grievance frameworks ensure accountability and reinforce a safe, respectful, and inclusive workplace culture. Employees, workers, and external stakeholders, including customers and suppliers, have access to multiple reporting channels, such as the whistleblower mechanism (toll-free number, email, and written communication), to raise concerns regarding any actual or potential violations. All grievances received are formally reviewed, investigated, and addressed through designated committees, including the Ethics Committee and Grievance Redressal Committee, depending on the nature of the concern. ; To maintain high level of legal, ethical, and moral standard, the Company has a Whistle Blower Policy and established vigil mechanism. No personnel has been denied access to the Chairman of the Audit Committee during the year under review. The Whistle Blower Policy has been communicated to all and posted on the Company's website www.demomanufacturing.example."
