      "highlights": "Mazars Advisory LLP is engaged as an independent agency to conduct the impact assessment of DML CSR projects for the financial year 2023-2024. The core responsibilities include: (a) Objective Evaluation: Assessment of effectiveness, outcomes, and sustainability of Escort Demo Manufacturing Ltd CSR projects, including agricultural training, skill development, environmental initiatives, and institutional development. (b) Methodology: Using of structured approach including stakeholder consultations, beneficiary sampling, data collection, field visits, and analysis of both qualitative and quantitative indicators to measure the impact of each CSR intervention. (c) Reporting: Preparation of a comprehensive report detailing the extent to which project objectives were met, the tangible and intangible benefits realized by beneficiaries, and the broader social, economic, and environmental impacts. (d) Recommendations: Providing of actionable insights and recommendations to Escort Demo Manufacturing Ltd for enhancing the design, implementation, and monitoring of future CSR initiatives, ensuring alignment with statutory requirements and best practices in impact assessment. (e) Compliance: Ensuring that the assessment process and reporting adhered to the requirements of Section 135 of the Companies Act, 2013, and relevant CSR rules, which mandate third-party impact assessments for projects above specified thresholds."
