      "metrics": [],
      "highlights": "DML adopts a proactive and integrated approach to risk management to strengthen organisational resilience and support long-term value creation. The Company continuously assesses evolving business, operational, financial, technological, and sustainability-related risks to enhance preparedness, improve responsiveness, and ensure business continuity; Enterprise Risk Management (ERM) at DML refers to the holistic and continuous process of identifying, assessing, managing, and monitoring risks across the organisation to ensure the achievement of strategic and operational objectives. It is embedded within business decision-making and covers all categories of risks, including strategic, operational, financial, and compliance risks. ERM enables the Company to proactively address uncertainties, improve resilience, and enhance performance by aligning risk-taking with defined risk appetite. Through structured governance involving the Board, Risk Management Committee, Chief Risk Officer, and Risk Owners, ERM ensures accountability, transparency, and integration of risk considerations into everyday operations and long-term planning. The Enterprise Risk Management Framework, on the other hand, represents the structured architecture and methodology through which ERM is implemented within the organisation. It provides the guiding principles, processes, tools, and governance mechanisms that enable systematic risk management. At DML, the framework—aligned with the COSO model—includes components such as internal environment, objective setting, event identification, risk assessment, risk response, control activities, communication, and monitoring. While ERM defines what the organisation seeks to achieve in managing risks, the framework defines how this is operationalised, ensuring consistency, repeatability, and effectiveness in managing risks across all functions and business units."
