      "highlights": "DML’s Double Materiality Assessment has been developed in alignment with ESRS 1 & ESRS 2 principles, GRI 3: Material Topics, industrial benchmarking, internal risk documents, ensuring a structured and globally consistent approach to identifying sustainability priorities. Identification of Material Topics: A comprehensive list of ESG topics was developed based on global standards, peer analysis, and internal frameworks to capture all relevant sustainability issues; Identification of IROs (Impacts, Risks, Opportunities): Each topic was evaluated to identify potential environmental, social, and governance impacts, as well as financial risks and opportunities; Stakeholder Engagement: Key stakeholders were engaged through structured surveys to assess both impact and financial relevance of each topic; Assessing Impact and Financial Materiality: Topics were quantitatively scored using ESRS-aligned methodologies for impact and financial materiality, applying weighting, normalisation, and bias adjustment; Double Materiality Matrix Development: Scores were plotted on a two-dimensional graph to visualise priority topics based on impact and financial significance."
