      "highlights": "Human & Labour Rights: In line with its ethical values, DML upholds human rights and labour standards across its operations and value chain through a strengthened Human Rights Due Diligence (HRDD) approach aligned with global frameworks such as the UN Guiding Principles and UN Global Compact. The Company continues to expand the scope and effectiveness of these assessments to enhance accountability and responsible business conduct; DML remains committed to upholding human rights, ethical labour practices, and responsible business conduct across its operations and value chain. During FY 2025-26, the Company advanced its human rights governance journey by progressing towards a formal Human Rights Policy aligned with leading global frameworks, including the UN Guiding Principles, OECD guidelines and ILO Core Conventions. These efforts are supported by established governance mechanisms that promote ethical practices, nondiscrimination, and protection of fundamental rights for all stakeholders, reinforcing DML’s commitment to responsible and transparent business practices."
