      "highlights": "Renewable Energy: We are working towards tripling the share of renewable energy in our energy mix by FY 2029-30, compared to FY 2022-23 levels. There is a increasing trend in renewable energy consumption from FY 2022-23 to FY 2025-26. The increase during FY 2023-24 reflects our initial progress towards greater renewable energy adoption, while the temporary decline in FY 2024-25 is due to operational changes particularly the non-functioning solar plant. During FY 2025-26, increased procurement of renewable energy through the Indian Energy Exchange (IEX), complemented by energy-efficient technologies and process optimisation initiatives, led to higher renewable energy consumption compared to FY 2024-25, reflecting continued progress towards our energy transition and efficiency goals. Our renewable energy consumption increased from 4.53 TJ in FY 2022-23 to 9.47 TJ in FY 2025-26, representing an overall increase of 109.05% and more than double over the period."
