      "metrics": [],
      "highlights": "Gender Diversity: DML Targets 15% gender diversity from employee category by 2031. There is steady and consistent increase in women’s representation across all four years. During FY 2025–26, it reached to 8.74% in which various wellness programmes, engagement initiatives, and support systems were strengthened to promote a positive work environment. We are making consistent and meaningful progress in improving gender diversity in the workforce. Women’s representation rises from baseline year FY 2022‑23 (5%) to FY 2025-26 (8.74%). This is an overall 74.8% increase, a substantial improvement over the period; In FY 2025-26, we intensified our focus on building a diverse and inclusive workplace, with particular emphasis on women and young talent. Gradually, we have increased the intake of young professionals from campuses, along with improving gender diversity achieving more than 40% female representation within this group, supporting the company's focused efforts towards enhancing women’s participation in operational role. Overall gender diversity among permanent and contractual white-collar employees improved from 8.0% to 8.74%."
