      "metrics": [],
      "highlights": "Market served by the entity: (a) Number of locations: National (No. of States): 28 states and 8 Union Territories; International (No. of Countries): 71; (b) The contribution of exports as a percentage of the total turnover of the entity: 5.54%; (c) Brief on types of customers: Demo Manufacturing Limited (DML) serves a diverse customer base across agriculture and construction sectors, focusing on delivering reliable, safe, and accessible solutions that enhance productivity and support sustainable development. The Company adopts a customer-centric approach by addressing varied needs across geographies, income segments, and end-use applications. (1) Customer in Agri Machinery Product Segment: DML caters to stakeholders across the agricultural value chain, including small and marginal farmers, large farm owners, farmer producer organizations (FPOs), cooperatives, rural entrepreneurs, and institutional customers in domestic and international markets. The Company provides end-to-end farm mechanization solutions spanning the crop cycle from land preparation to harvesting. Its product portfolio includes tractors, transplanters, harvesters, implements, engines, and related components under Demo Manufacturing, Farmtrac, Powertrac, Demo Manufacturing, Steeltrac, Farmpower, and E Demo Manufacturing brands, designed to suit diverse agro-climatic conditions and farm sizes across more than 60 countries. DML supports inclusive access through a wide dealer and service network, ensuring last-mile connectivity, after-sales service, and customer awareness, thereby contributing to improved farm productivity and rural livelihoods. (2) Customer in Construction Equipment Segment: DML serves a diverse set of customers engaged in infrastructure and industrial development, including construction and engineering companies, government and public sector agencies, mining operators, rental and leasing companies, and individual contractors. The Company’s construction equipment portfolio are marketed under the Demo Manufacturing and Demo Manufacturing brands; comprises material handling cranes, road compaction machinery, and earthmoving equipment, contributing to the development of critical sectors such as infrastructure, mining, cement, power, etc. With over 250 customer touchpoints across India and a presence in more than 30 countries, DML ensures strong product accessibility, service support, and continuous customer engagement. The Company places a strong emphasis on safety, reliability, and lifecycle performance, while systematically integrating customer feedback to enhance product quality, operational efficiency, and overall customer experience."
